    "body": "Fish has Vi key bindings.\nSo normally while I’m using the shell I’m in ‘insert mode’.  \nWhen I press `Escape`, I enter ‘normal mode’. In this Mode, Keypresses don’t insert Text but move the cursor etc.\n\nThe prompt changes depending on the mode I’m in.\n\nSome prompts show `[I]` and `[N]`, Starship and Spaceship just turn around the Prompt Character.\n\nHowever in Kitty, pressing Escape doesn’t do what I expect.\n\nIt creates a new prompt line with the prompt character tinted around, it doesn’t stay in the current prompt line.\n\nWhat happened between the lines in the screenshot above was just pressing Escape.\nExpected behavior would be to ONLY turn around the prompt character.\n\nThis (getting a new prompt line) also happens with Starship when I’m pasting from Clipboard in Kitty!\n\nWith iTerm I had different problems with Starship and Vi Mode: https://github.com/starship/starship/issues/1246",
    "author_association": "NONE",
